# {{ project_name }} backend

FastAPI service with two API surfaces: `/api/admin` (admin frontend) and `/api/v1` (public, mobile).
Conventions and architecture are in `AGENTS.md`.

## Quickstart

```sh
cp .env.example .env
# set APP_JWT_SECRET (at least 32 bytes): openssl rand -hex 32
make up
make migrate
make create-admin ARGS="--email you@example.com"   # prompts for the password (hidden)
```

`make up` builds and starts db, redis, Grafana (otel-lgtm), api, worker and scheduler on
loopback ports. `make migrate` runs Alembic from your host against the compose database.

- Admin API docs: http://localhost:8000/api/admin/docs
- Public API docs: http://localhost:8000/api/v1/docs
- Grafana (logs, traces, metrics): http://localhost:3000

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
| ------- | ------------ |
| `make dev` | Run the API with reload on port 8000 |
| `make lint` | ruff check, ruff format check, ty |
| `make fmt` | Format and autofix with ruff |
| `make test` | Run pytest (needs Docker for testcontainers) |
| `make check` | `make lint` plus `make test` |
| `make openapi` | Export `openapi/admin.json` and `openapi/public.json` |
| `make up` | Start the compose stack and wait until healthy |
| `make down` | Stop the compose stack |
| `make migrate` | Apply migrations (`alembic upgrade head`) |
| `make migration m="message"` | Autogenerate a new migration |
| `make create-admin ARGS="--email you@example.com"` | Create an admin user; `--email` is required, the password is prompted |

## Environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env`. All `APP_*` keys are read by `app.core.config.Settings`.

| Key | Purpose |
| --- | ------- |
| `APP_ENV` | `dev`, `test` or `prod` |
| `APP_DATABASE_URL` | Postgres URL (`postgresql+asyncpg://...`) |
| `APP_REDIS_URL` | Redis URL for rate limiting and the task broker |
| `APP_JWT_SECRET` | JWT signing secret, at least 32 bytes, no default |
| `APP_COOKIE_SECURE` | `true` marks the refresh cookie `Secure`; must be `true` in deploys |
| `APP_CORS_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated list of allowed origins |
| `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` | OTLP gRPC endpoint for traces and metrics |
| `OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` | Service name reported to OpenTelemetry |
| `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` | Proxy IPs uvicorn trusts for `X-Forwarded-*`; read by uvicorn, not `Settings` |

## Deploy

- Serve the admin frontend and this API from the same site behind one reverse proxy. The refresh
  cookie is `SameSite=Strict`, so a cross-site admin origin cannot use it.
- Set `FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS` to the reverse proxy IPs so client IPs (rate limiting) are correct.
- Set `APP_COOKIE_SECURE=true` and serve over HTTPS.
- Run `make migrate` (or the compose `migrate` service) before starting a new version.
- Run the worker and scheduler as separate processes next to the API.
